	"department": "KINES",
	"description": [
		"This course will explore the different time periods in a woman's life starting at puberty, the time around pregnancy, perimenopause, and post menopause. Changes in hormones lead to potential challenges for sleep, nutrition, exercise, and general health. As women approach mid-life, the risk of chronic disease significantly increases potentially leading to a poorer quality of life. Prevention strategies relating to wellness, nutrition, and exercise will be discussed. Prerequisite: declared kinesiology major."
